{
	"version": 3,
	"doc": "docs/02 §8 — phrase/regex pre-pass lists for Safety.gd (SafetyFilter). Matching is obfuscation-resistant: zero-width and combining chars are stripped, Latin/Greek/Cyrillic homoglyphs and common leet substitutions are folded, and phrases match on a whitespace-free AND separator-free compact view, so `k#ll`, `k~ll`, `ki•ll`, `kill • yourself` and `kill~yourself` all collapse onto `killyourself` (SAF-14/CODE-13); the kill regexes use a tolerant [^0-9A-Za-z] delimiter class with i-or-l interior slots so `1`-as-`l` obfuscations (`ki1l`, `ki11`, `kiIl` — folded to `kiil`/`kiii`) still match (CODE-17), and personal_data regexes accept a repeated non-word separator between digit groups (`555~0134~5678`, `555--0134--5678`, `mika@example~com`) instead of requiring -/./spaces (CODE-20); the IPv4 and coordinate-pair arms stay narrow — the separator must repeat and may not be `,` or `:`, so decimal and time chains (`90.00,80.00`, `10:30,11:15`, `100,200,300,400`) are not personal data (CODE-22/SAF-18), and the DMS arm is lowercase because it runs on the normalized view (`41°00'N`). The threat kill arm needs a person-shaped target after `all` (`kill all of them`, `kill all the jews`) or an object-free `kill all` ending a clause; tool idioms (`kill all the lights`, `kill all bugs`, `killall bots`) stay clean (SAF-16). Verb inflection belongs to the kill stem: every kill arm carries an inflection slot after its final kill letter and before the delimiter class — `(?:[^0-9A-Za-z]{0,3}(?:s|ed|ing|ng|ss))?` on the `all` arms, the required form of the same group on the self-directed and pronoun-subject arms — so `kills all the jews`, `killed all of them`, `killing all the blacks`, `kill!s all the jews`, `kill,ed all of them`, `kill!ng all humans` and the `$`→`s` fold `kill$s` all block exactly like the base forms; a separator between the stem and the suffix (`kill!s`, `kill,ed`) is treated exactly like an in-stem separator (`k!lls`), so the stem-suffix boundary cannot hide the conjugation (SAF-19/SAF-23); the target-pronoun arm itself stays uninflected because a derived subject makes the same surface a benign idiom (`the job kills you slowly`, `criticism kills self-esteem`), so the inflected form is caught only when a pronoun subject owns it (`i killed you`, `he kills her`) — the harmful shape is first person, not a description; that pronoun-subject arm resets its match start to the verb with `\\K` after its subject and aux slots, so the span never swallows a negator and `_negated` reads `i never killed you`, `she never killed him`, `we never killed them`, `you never killed her` as negated exactly like the bare-kill arm reads `i did not kill you`, while `i killed you` and `i always killed you` still block (SAF-22); the self-directed forms get their own narrow arms with a required inflection slot (`i almost killed myself`, `you killed yourself`) because `me` itself must stay uninflected — `killing me`/`killed me` are benign idioms the corpus pins. Regexes run on the normalized view (PCRE2 via Godot RegEx). Streaming holds pending text by the longest phrase (measured on the compact views) plus any trailing token or hold_pattern match, so a phrase or unbounded regex (coordinates, phone, email) can never complete after a partially emitted prefix, and cross-beat state carries the previous beat's displayed tail so a phrase split across say beats is still caught — including splits at separator-class clause breaks like `,` or `!` (CODE-2/CODE-14/CODE-18). negation_guard is narrow: exactly one negator in the clause, and only auxiliaries/pronouns/coordinated already-covered phrases may sit between it and the match; anything ambiguous stays blocked. negation_exempt lists harmful phrases whose own wording contains a negator (e.g. \"i don't want to live\") and must still block. script_guard redacts output in scripts this list cannot scan (CJK, Cyrillic, Arabic, ...). personal_data is the only player-exempt, plain-view category. `probes` gives one string per category that the loader must actually catch, so a compiled-but-inert rule group fails the load closed (CODE-16).",
	"gate": { "min_stage": 4, "content_level": "full" },
